IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sgd-compromise`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: Part 7, ss 215A to 215H and 215K (amalgamations).
-- The solvency statements of ss 215I and 215J are in sgd-amalgamation-solvency.l4.
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes a person's point of view; the seat layer (sgd-seat.l4) does.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29 and the Guide's rulings; see NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (sgd)").
--   JUST TRUE   the section's own test is met on the facts given.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no to this case in its own words (a "means" definition, a condition introduced by "if", "unless",
--               "until"; a list closed with "only"; a flat negative; a period or "where" condition the text states).
--   NOTHING     not covered: the text lists without closing the list, says "includes", is silent, points to a power or
--               instrument outside the sources, or limits a grant in its own wording and the case falls outside the limit.
--   A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Every branch that answers no carries `-- FALSE-kind (...)`; every branch that answers "not covered" carries `-- NOTHING-kind (...)`.
-- Periods are counted only by sg-periods.l4 (conventions P1 to P9 of the keel: assumed, not ruled by a lawyer).
-- A day is a DATE, written Date day month year. "Before the general meeting" is judged on days alone: an act on an earlier day is before it,
-- an act on a later day is not, and an act on the day of the meeting cannot be placed from a date (NOTHING; fork F-215C-1).
-- The board of directors is a party the core's `Party` does not have: this module declares one of its own (NEEDS-CORE.md).
-- The Official Receiver is the party `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver`, declared once in sgd-compromise.l4 at its first use.

§ `Section 215A: amalgamation`

-- Heading (line 21066): "Amalgamations": not operative.

DECLARE `s 215A the amalgamated company` IS ONE OF
    `s 215A one of the amalgamating companies`
    `s 215A a new company`
    `s 215A some other company`

GIVEN company IS A `s 215A the amalgamated company`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 215A the amalgamated company is one of the amalgamating companies or a new company` MEANS
    CONSIDER company
    WHEN `s 215A one of the amalgamating companies` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 215A a new company` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- 215A: "Without affecting section 212 and any other law relating to the merger or amalgamation of companies, 2 or more companies may amalgamate and continue as one company, which may be one of the amalgamating
-- companies or a new company, in accordance with sections 215B to 215G, where applicable." A grant ("may") limited by its own wording: the case outside it answers NOTHING (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-215A-1).
-- src:21068 | 215A. Without affecting section 212 and any other law relating to
-- src:21069 | the merger or amalgamation of companies, 2 or more companies may
-- src:21070 | amalgamate and continue as one company, which may be one of the
-- src:21071 | amalgamating companies or a new company, in accordance with
-- src:21072 | sections 215B to 215G, where applicable.
@ref s 215A (src:21068-21072)
GIVEN `the number of companies that amalgamate` IS A NUMBER
      company IS A `s 215A the amalgamated company`
      `the amalgamation is in accordance with sections 215B to 215G, where applicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215A the companies may amalgamate and continue as one company` MEANS
    IF    (`the number of companies that amalgamate` AT LEAST 2)
      AND `s 215A the amalgamated company is one of the amalgamating companies or a new company` company
      AND `the amalgamation is in accordance with sections 215B to 215G, where applicable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "2 or more companies may amalgamate and continue as one company, which may be one of the amalgamating companies or a new company, in accordance with sections 215B to 215G, where applicable" (a grant naming 2 or more companies, two kinds of amalgamated company and the manner; grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-215A-1)

§ `Section 215B: the amalgamation proposal`

-- Heading (line 21074): "Amalgamation proposal": not operative.

-- What the proposal contains, item by item, as a reader of the proposal could state it. Three items are conditional: (g) and (h) bite only where the proposal has the case they speak of.
DECLARE `s 215B(1) what the proposal contains` HAS
    `s 215B(1)(a) the name of the amalgamated company is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215B(1)(b) the registered office of the amalgamated company is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215B(1)(c) the full name of every director of the amalgamated company is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215B(1)(ca) the residential address and contact address of every director of the amalgamated company which is contained in the register of directors kept by the Registrar under section 173(1)(a) are stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215B(1)(d)(i) the number of shares of the amalgamated company is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215B(1)(d)(ii) the rights, privileges, limitations and conditions attached to each share of the amalgamated company are stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215B(1)(d)(iii) whether the shares are transferable or non-transferable and, if transferable, whether their transfer is subject to any condition or limitation, is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215B(1)(e) a copy of the constitution of the amalgamated company is included` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215B(1)(f) the manner in which the shares of each amalgamating company are to be converted into shares of the amalgamated company is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215B(1)(g) shares of an amalgamating company are not to be converted into shares of the amalgamated company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215B(1)(g) the consideration that the holders of those shares are to receive instead is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215B(1)(h) a payment is to be made to a member or director of an amalgamating company, other than a payment of the kind described in paragraph (g)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215B(1)(h) that payment is stated` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 215B(1)(i) details of any arrangement necessary to complete the amalgamation and to provide for the subsequent management and operation of the amalgamated company are stated` IS A BOOLEAN

-- (1): "An amalgamation proposal must contain the terms of an amalgamation under section 215A and, in particular — (a) ...; (i) details of any arrangement necessary to complete the amalgamation". A duty: the provision's own question.
-- src:21076 | 215B.—(1) An amalgamation proposal must contain the terms of
-- src:21077 | an amalgamation under section 215A and, in particular —
-- src:21079 | (a) the name of the amalgamated company;
-- src:21081 | (b) the registered office of the amalgamated company;
-- src:21083 | (c) the full name of every director of the amalgamated
-- src:21084 | company;
-- src:21089 | (ca) the residential address and contact address of every
-- src:21090 | director of the amalgamated company which is contained
-- src:21091 | in the register of directors kept by the Registrar under
-- src:21092 | section 173(1)(a) in respect of the company;
-- src:21096 | (d) the share structure of the amalgamated company,
-- src:21097 | specifying —
-- src:21099 | (i) the number of shares of the amalgamated company;
-- src:21101 | (ii) the rights, privileges, limitations and conditions
-- src:21102 | attached to each share of the amalgamated
-- src:21103 | company; and
-- src:21105 | (iii) whether the shares are transferable or
-- src:21106 | non‑transferable and, if transferable, whether their
-- src:21107 | transfer is subject to any condition or limitation;
-- src:21109 | (e) a copy of the constitution of the amalgamated company;
-- src:21111 | (f) the manner in which the shares of each amalgamating
-- src:21112 | company are to be converted into shares of the
-- src:21113 | amalgamated company;
-- src:21115 | (g) if shares of an amalgamating company are not to be
-- src:21116 | converted into shares of the amalgamated company, the
-- src:21117 | consideration that the holders of those shares are to receive
-- src:21118 | instead of shares of the amalgamated company;
-- src:21120 | (h) any payment to be made to any member or director of an
-- src:21121 | amalgamating company, other than a payment of the kind
-- src:21122 | described in paragraph (g); and
-- src:21124 | (i) details of any arrangement necessary to complete the
-- src:21125 | amalgamation and to provide for the subsequent
-- src:21126 | management and operation of the amalgamated company.
@ref s 215B(1) (src:21076-21126)
GIVEN contents IS A `s 215B(1) what the proposal contains`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215B(1) the amalgamation proposal contains what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    (contents's `s 215B(1)(a) the name of the amalgamated company is stated`)
      AND (contents's `s 215B(1)(b) the registered office of the amalgamated company is stated`)
      AND (contents's `s 215B(1)(c) the full name of every director of the amalgamated company is stated`)
      AND (contents's `s 215B(1)(ca) the residential address and contact address of every director of the amalgamated company which is contained in the register of directors kept by the Registrar under section 173(1)(a) are stated`)
      AND (contents's `s 215B(1)(d)(i) the number of shares of the amalgamated company is stated`)
      AND (contents's `s 215B(1)(d)(ii) the rights, privileges, limitations and conditions attached to each share of the amalgamated company are stated`)
      AND (contents's `s 215B(1)(d)(iii) whether the shares are transferable or non-transferable and, if transferable, whether their transfer is subject to any condition or limitation, is stated`)
      AND (contents's `s 215B(1)(e) a copy of the constitution of the amalgamated company is included`)
      AND (contents's `s 215B(1)(f) the manner in which the shares of each amalgamating company are to be converted into shares of the amalgamated company is stated`)
      AND ((NOT (contents's `s 215B(1)(g) shares of an amalgamating company are not to be converted into shares of the amalgamated company`)) OR (contents's `s 215B(1)(g) the consideration that the holders of those shares are to receive instead is stated`))
      AND ((NOT (contents's `s 215B(1)(h) a payment is to be made to a member or director of an amalgamating company, other than a payment of the kind described in paragraph (g)`)) OR (contents's `s 215B(1)(h) that payment is stated`))
      AND (contents's `s 215B(1)(i) details of any arrangement necessary to complete the amalgamation and to provide for the subsequent management and operation of the amalgamated company are stated`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An amalgamation proposal must contain the terms of an amalgamation under section 215A and, in particular —" (a duty not met; the provision's own question; a proposal missing a listed item does not contain what the subsection requires)

-- (2): "An amalgamation proposal may specify the date on which the amalgamation is intended to become effective." A grant limited by its own wording: NOTHING outside it (fork F-215B-1).
-- src:21130 | (2) An amalgamation proposal may specify the date on which the
-- src:21131 | amalgamation is intended to become effective.
@ref s 215B(2) (src:21130-21131)
GIVEN `the document is an amalgamation proposal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date specified is the date on which the amalgamation is intended to become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215B(2) the amalgamation proposal may specify the date` MEANS
    IF `the document is an amalgamation proposal` AND `the date specified is the date on which the amalgamation is intended to become effective`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An amalgamation proposal may specify the date on which the amalgamation is intended to become effective" (a grant naming one thing; grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-215B-1)

-- (3): "If shares of one of the amalgamating companies are held by or on behalf of another of the amalgamating companies, the amalgamation proposal (a) must provide for the cancellation of those shares without payment or the provision
-- of other consideration when the amalgamation becomes effective; and (b) must not provide for the conversion of those shares into shares of the amalgamated company."
-- src:21133 | (3) If shares of one of the amalgamating companies are held by or
-- src:21134 | on behalf of another of the amalgamating companies, the
-- src:21135 | amalgamation proposal —
-- src:21140 | (a) must provide for the cancellation of those shares without
-- src:21141 | payment or the provision of other consideration when the
-- src:21142 | amalgamation becomes effective; and
-- src:21144 | (b) must not provide for the conversion of those shares into
-- src:21145 | shares of the amalgamated company.
@ref s 215B(3) (src:21133-21145)
GIVEN `shares of one of the amalgamating companies are held by or on behalf of another of the amalgamating companies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal provides for the cancellation of those shares without payment or the provision of other consideration when the amalgamation becomes effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proposal provides for the conversion of those shares into shares of the amalgamated company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215B(3) the amalgamation proposal provides as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `shares of one of the amalgamating companies are held by or on behalf of another of the amalgamating companies`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If shares of one of the amalgamating companies are held by or on behalf of another of the amalgamating companies, the amalgamation proposal" (a condition introduced by "if"; the duty arises only on it; marginal reading (a))
    ELSE IF `the proposal provides for the cancellation of those shares without payment or the provision of other consideration when the amalgamation becomes effective` AND (NOT `the proposal provides for the conversion of those shares into shares of the amalgamated company`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) must provide for the cancellation of those shares without payment ...; and (b) must not provide for the conversion of those shares" (a duty and a prohibition not met; the provision's own question)

-- (4): "A cancellation of shares under this section is not deemed to be a reduction of share capital within the meaning of this Act." A flat negative.
-- src:21147 | (4) A cancellation of shares under this section is not deemed to be a
-- src:21148 | reduction of share capital within the meaning of this Act.
@ref s 215B(4) (src:21147-21148)
GIVEN `the cancellation of the shares is a cancellation under section 215B` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215B(4) the cancellation of the shares is deemed to be a reduction of share capital within the meaning of the Act` MEANS
    IF `the cancellation of the shares is a cancellation under section 215B`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A cancellation of shares under this section is not deemed to be a reduction of share capital within the meaning of this Act" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A cancellation of shares under this section" (the subsection speaks of cancellations under section 215B and says nothing of any other)

-- (5): "For the purposes of subsection (1)(a), the name of the amalgamated company may be (a) the name of one of the amalgamating companies; or (b) a new name that has been reserved under section 27(12B)."
DECLARE `s 215B(5) the name` IS ONE OF
    `s 215B(5)(a) the name of one of the amalgamating companies`
    `s 215B(5)(b) a new name`
    `s 215B(5) some other name`

-- src:21150 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (1)(a), the name of the
-- src:21151 | amalgamated company may be —
-- src:21153 | (a) the name of one of the amalgamating companies; or
-- src:21155 | (b) a new name that has been reserved under section 27(12B).
@ref s 215B(5) (src:21150-21155)
GIVEN name IS A `s 215B(5) the name`
      `the new name has been reserved under section 27(12B)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215B(5) the name may be the name of the amalgamated company` MEANS
    CONSIDER name
    WHEN `s 215B(5)(a) the name of one of the amalgamating companies` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 215B(5)(b) a new name` THEN
        IF `the new name has been reserved under section 27(12B)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) a new name that has been reserved under section 27(12B)" (a grant limited to a reserved name; grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-215B-2)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the name of the amalgamated company may be — (a) the name of one of the amalgamating companies; or (b) a new name that has been reserved" (a grant naming two kinds of name and no other; fork F-215B-2)

§ `Section 215C: the manner of approving the proposal`

-- Heading (line 21159): "Manner of approving amalgamation proposal": not operative.

-- "by special resolution at a general meeting": the core's kinds of resolution and of meeting; a general meeting is an annual or an extraordinary general meeting.
GIVEN resolution IS A `Kind of resolution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 215C(1)(a) the resolution is a special resolution` MEANS
    CONSIDER resolution
    WHEN `a special resolution` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN meeting IS A `Kind of meeting`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 215C(1)(a) the meeting is a general meeting` MEANS
    CONSIDER meeting
    WHEN `an annual general meeting` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an extraordinary general meeting` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- (1): "An amalgamation proposal must be approved (a) subject to the constitution of each amalgamating company, by the members of each amalgamating company by special resolution at a general meeting; and
-- (b) by any other person, where any provision in the amalgamation proposal would, if contained in any amendment to the constitution of an amalgamating company or otherwise proposed in relation to that company, require the approval of that person."
-- src:21161 | 215C.—(1) An amalgamation proposal must be approved —
-- src:21163 | (a) subject to the constitution of each amalgamating company,
-- src:21164 | by the members of each amalgamating company by special
-- src:21165 | resolution at a general meeting; and
-- src:21167 | (b) by any other person, where any provision in the
-- src:21168 | amalgamation proposal would, if contained in any
-- src:21169 | amendment to the constitution of an amalgamating
-- src:21170 | company or otherwise proposed in relation to that
-- src:21171 | company, require the approval of that person.
@ref s 215C(1) (src:21161-21171)
GIVEN resolution IS A `Kind of resolution`
      meeting IS A `Kind of meeting`
      `the constitution of each amalgamating company is complied with in the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision in the amalgamation proposal would, if contained in an amendment to the constitution of an amalgamating company or otherwise proposed in relation to that company, require the approval of a person other than the members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that other person has approved the amalgamation proposal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215C(1) the amalgamation proposal has been approved as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `s 215C(1)(a) the resolution is a special resolution` resolution
      AND `s 215C(1)(a) the meeting is a general meeting` meeting
      AND `the constitution of each amalgamating company is complied with in the approval`
      AND ((NOT `a provision in the amalgamation proposal would, if contained in an amendment to the constitution of an amalgamating company or otherwise proposed in relation to that company, require the approval of a person other than the members`) OR `that other person has approved the amalgamation proposal`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An amalgamation proposal must be approved — (a) subject to the constitution of each amalgamating company, by the members of each amalgamating company by special resolution at a general meeting; and (b) by any other person, where any provision in the amalgamation proposal would" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)

-- The day of the act and the day of the general meeting: "before the general meeting". An earlier day is before it; a later day is not; the same day cannot be placed from dates alone (fork F-215C-1).
-- src:21175 | (2) The board of directors of each amalgamating company must,
-- src:21176 | before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) —
-- src:21178 | (a) resolve that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the
-- src:21179 | amalgamating company;
-- src:21181 | (b) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating
-- src:21182 | company in accordance with section 215I; and
-- src:21184 | (c) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated
-- src:21185 | company in accordance with section 215J.
@ref s 215C(2) before the meeting (src:21175-21185)
GIVEN `the day the act was done` IS A DATE
      `the day of the general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215C(2) the day is before the day of the general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the day the act was done` LESS THAN `the day of the general meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `the day the act was done` GREATER THAN `the day of the general meeting`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a)" (a duty with a stated time, not met; the provision's own question)
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "before the general meeting" (an act on the day of the meeting may be before it or after it; a date does not say; fork F-215C-1)

-- (2): "The board of directors of each amalgamating company must, before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) — (a) resolve that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the amalgamating company; (b) make a solvency statement
-- in relation to the amalgamating company in accordance with section 215I; and (c) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company in accordance with section 215J."
-- src:21175 | (2) The board of directors of each amalgamating company must,
-- src:21176 | before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) —
-- src:21178 | (a) resolve that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the
-- src:21179 | amalgamating company;
-- src:21181 | (b) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating
-- src:21182 | company in accordance with section 215I; and
-- src:21184 | (c) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated
-- src:21185 | company in accordance with section 215J.
@ref s 215C(2)(a) (src:21175-21185)
GIVEN `the board resolved that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the amalgamating company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the board so resolved` IS A DATE
      `the day of the general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215C(2)(a) the board resolved before the general meeting that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the amalgamating company` MEANS
    IF NOT `the board resolved that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the amalgamating company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must, before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) — (a) resolve that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the amalgamating company" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)
    ELSE `s 215C(2) the day is before the day of the general meeting` `the day the board so resolved` `the day of the general meeting`

-- src:21175 | (2) The board of directors of each amalgamating company must,
-- src:21176 | before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) —
-- src:21178 | (a) resolve that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the
-- src:21179 | amalgamating company;
-- src:21181 | (b) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating
-- src:21182 | company in accordance with section 215I; and
-- src:21184 | (c) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated
-- src:21185 | company in accordance with section 215J.
@ref s 215C(2)(b) (src:21175-21185)
GIVEN `the board made a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating company in accordance with section 215I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the board made it` IS A DATE
      `the day of the general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215C(2)(b) the board made the solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating company before the general meeting` MEANS
    IF NOT `the board made a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating company in accordance with section 215I`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating company in accordance with section 215I" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)
    ELSE `s 215C(2) the day is before the day of the general meeting` `the day the board made it` `the day of the general meeting`

-- src:21175 | (2) The board of directors of each amalgamating company must,
-- src:21176 | before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) —
-- src:21178 | (a) resolve that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the
-- src:21179 | amalgamating company;
-- src:21181 | (b) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating
-- src:21182 | company in accordance with section 215I; and
-- src:21184 | (c) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated
-- src:21185 | company in accordance with section 215J.
@ref s 215C(2)(c) (src:21175-21185)
GIVEN `the board made a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company in accordance with section 215J` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the board made it` IS A DATE
      `the day of the general meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215C(2)(c) the board made the solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company before the general meeting` MEANS
    IF NOT `the board made a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company in accordance with section 215J`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company in accordance with section 215J" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)
    ELSE `s 215C(2) the day is before the day of the general meeting` `the day the board made it` `the day of the general meeting`

-- The last day certain to be before the meeting, as a number of days after a start day (for the traces of the duties of subsections (2) and 215D(5)): the day before the meeting.
GIVEN `the day of the general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215C(2) the number of days from the start day to the day before the general meeting` MEANS
    (`period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the day of the general meeting` 1 Days) MINUS `the start day of the trace`

-- (3): "Every director who votes in favour of the resolution and the making of the statements mentioned in subsection (2) must sign a declaration stating (a) that, in his or her opinion, the conditions specified in subsection (2)(a),
-- section 215I(1)(a) and (b) (in relation to the amalgamating company) and section 215J(1)(a) and (b) (in relation to the amalgamated company) are satisfied; and (b) the grounds for that opinion."
-- src:21190 | (3) Every director who votes in favour of the resolution and the
-- src:21191 | making of the statements mentioned in subsection (2) must sign a
-- src:21192 | declaration stating —
-- src:21194 | (a) that, in his or her opinion, the conditions specified in
-- src:21195 | subsection (2)(a), section 215I(1)(a) and (b) (in relation to
-- src:21196 | the amalgamating company) and section 215J(1)(a) and (b)
-- src:21197 | (in relation to the amalgamated company) are satisfied; and
-- src:21199 | (b) the grounds for that opinion.
@ref s 215C(3) (src:21190-21199)
GIVEN `the director votes in favour of the resolution and the making of the statements mentioned in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215C(3) the director must sign the declaration` MEANS
    IF `the director votes in favour of the resolution and the making of the statements mentioned in subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Every director who votes in favour of the resolution and the making of the statements mentioned in subsection (2) must sign a declaration" (a duty that arises only for the director who so votes; periods ruling (b), marginal reading (a))

-- src:21190 | (3) Every director who votes in favour of the resolution and the
-- src:21191 | making of the statements mentioned in subsection (2) must sign a
-- src:21192 | declaration stating —
-- src:21194 | (a) that, in his or her opinion, the conditions specified in
-- src:21195 | subsection (2)(a), section 215I(1)(a) and (b) (in relation to
-- src:21196 | the amalgamating company) and section 215J(1)(a) and (b)
-- src:21197 | (in relation to the amalgamated company) are satisfied; and
-- src:21199 | (b) the grounds for that opinion.
@ref s 215C(3) content (src:21190-21199)
GIVEN `the declaration states that, in the director's opinion, the conditions specified in subsection (2)(a), section 215I(1)(a) and (b) and section 215J(1)(a) and (b) are satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the declaration states the grounds for that opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215C(3) the declaration states what the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the declaration states that, in the director's opinion, the conditions specified in subsection (2)(a), section 215I(1)(a) and (b) and section 215J(1)(a) and (b) are satisfied` AND `the declaration states the grounds for that opinion`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must sign a declaration stating — (a) that, in his or her opinion, the conditions specified ... are satisfied; and (b) the grounds for that opinion" (a duty not met; the provision's own question)

-- (4): "The board of directors of each amalgamating company must send to every member of the amalgamating company, not less than 21 days before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) — (a) a copy of the amalgamation proposal;
-- (b) a copy of the declarations given by the directors under subsection (3); (c) a statement of any material interests of the directors ...; and (d) such further information and explanation as may be necessary".
-- "not less than 21 days before": the last day is the day of the meeting less 21 (P5).
-- src:21201 | (4) The board of directors of each amalgamating company must
-- src:21202 | send to every member of the amalgamating company, not less than
-- src:21203 | 21 days before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) —
-- src:21205 | (a) a copy of the amalgamation proposal;
-- src:21207 | (b) a copy of the declarations given by the directors under
-- src:21208 | subsection (3);
-- src:21210 | (c) a statement of any material interests of the directors,
-- src:21211 | whether in that capacity or otherwise; and
-- src:21213 | (d) such further information and explanation as may be
-- src:21214 | necessary to enable a reasonable member of the
-- src:21215 | amalgamating company to understand the nature and
-- src:21216 | implications, for the amalgamating company and its
-- src:21217 | members, of the proposed amalgamation.
@ref s 215C(4) (src:21201-21217)
GIVEN `the day of the general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the day the board sent them to every member` IS A DATE
      `the board sent a copy of the amalgamation proposal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board sent a copy of the declarations given by the directors under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board sent a statement of any material interests of the directors, whether in that capacity or otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the board sent such further information and explanation as may be necessary to enable a reasonable member to understand the nature and implications of the proposed amalgamation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215C(4) the board sent what the subsection requires to every member at least 21 days before the general meeting` MEANS
    IF    `the board sent a copy of the amalgamation proposal`
      AND `the board sent a copy of the declarations given by the directors under subsection (3)`
      AND `the board sent a statement of any material interests of the directors, whether in that capacity or otherwise`
      AND `the board sent such further information and explanation as may be necessary to enable a reasonable member to understand the nature and implications of the proposed amalgamation`
      AND `period: the date is at least a period before` `the day the board sent them to every member` `the day of the general meeting` 21 Days
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must send to every member of the amalgamating company, not less than 21 days before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) — (a) a copy of the amalgamation proposal; (b) a copy of the declarations" (a duty with a stated period, not met; the provision's own question)

-- The last day for the sending, as a number of days after a start day (for the trace): the day of the meeting less 21 days.
GIVEN `the day of the general meeting` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215C(4) the number of days from the start day to the last day for the sending` MEANS
    (`period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the day of the general meeting` 21 Days) MINUS `the start day of the trace`

-- (5): "The directors of each amalgamating company must, not less than 21 days before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) — (a) send a copy of the amalgamation proposal to every secured creditor of the amalgamating company; and
-- (b) cause to be published in at least one daily English newspaper circulating generally in Singapore a notice of the proposed amalgamation, including a statement that (i) copies ... are available for inspection ...; and (ii) a member or creditor ... is entitled to be supplied free of charge".
