GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215D(8) the cancellation of the shares is deemed to be a reduction of share capital within the meaning of the Act` MEANS
    IF `the cancellation of the shares is a cancellation under section 215D`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A cancellation of shares under this section is not deemed to be a reduction of share capital within the meaning of this Act" (a flat negative)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A cancellation of shares under this section" (the subsection speaks of cancellations under section 215D and says nothing of any other)

§ `Section 215E: registration of the amalgamation`

-- Heading (line 21363): "Registration of amalgamation": not operative.

-- (1): "For the purpose of effecting an amalgamation, the following documents must be filed with the Registrar, in the prescribed form with such particulars as may be required in the form, together with payment of the prescribed fee: (a) the amalgamation
-- proposal that has been approved; (aa) any solvency statement made under section 215C(2) or 215D(5), as the case may be; (b) any declaration required under section 215C(3) or 215D(6); (c) a declaration signed by the directors of each amalgamating company ...;
-- (d) where the amalgamated company is a new company or the amalgamation proposal provides for a change of the name ..., a copy of any notice or other documentary evidence that the name ... has been reserved under section 27(12B); (e) a declaration signed by the directors, or proposed directors, of the
-- amalgamated company stating that, where the proportion of the claims of the creditors of the amalgamated company ... is greater than ..., no creditor will be prejudiced by that fact."
-- No party is named as the one who files, and no time is given: a duty with no named bearer (NOTES.md, "Rules with no breach path (sgd)"). The prescribed form and fee are outside the sources: inputs.
-- src:21365 | 215E.—(1) For the purpose of effecting an amalgamation, the
-- src:21366 | following documents must be filed with the Registrar, in the
-- src:21367 | prescribed form with such particulars as may be required in the
-- src:21368 | form, together with payment of the prescribed fee:
-- src:21370 | (a) the amalgamation proposal that has been approved;
-- src:21372 | (aa) any solvency statement made under section 215C(2) or
-- src:21373 | 215D(5), as the case may be;
-- src:21375 | (b) any declaration required under section 215C(3) or
-- src:21376 | 215D(6), as the case may be;
-- src:21378 | (c) a declaration signed by the directors of each amalgamating
-- src:21379 | company stating that the amalgamation has been approved
-- src:21384 | in accordance with this Act and the constitution of the
-- src:21385 | amalgamating company;
-- src:21387 | (d) where the amalgamated company is a new company or the
-- src:21388 | amalgamation proposal provides for a change of the name
-- src:21389 | of the amalgamated company, a copy of any notice or other
-- src:21390 | documentary evidence that the name which it is proposed
-- src:21391 | to be registered or the proposed new name (as the case may
-- src:21392 | be) has been reserved under section 27(12B);
-- src:21394 | (e) a declaration signed by the directors, or proposed directors,
-- src:21395 | of the amalgamated company stating that, where the
-- src:21396 | proportion of the claims of the creditors of the
-- src:21397 | amalgamated company in relation to the value of the
-- src:21398 | assets of the amalgamated company is greater than the
-- src:21399 | proportion of the claims of the creditors of an
-- src:21400 | amalgamating company in relation to the value of the
-- src:21401 | assets of the amalgamating company, no creditor will be
-- src:21402 | prejudiced by that fact.
@ref s 215E(1) (src:21365-21402)
GIVEN `the amalgamation proposal that has been approved is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any solvency statement made under section 215C(2) or 215D(5), as the case may be, is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any declaration required under section 215C(3) or 215D(6), as the case may be, is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a declaration signed by the directors of each amalgamating company stating that the amalgamation has been approved in accordance with this Act and the constitution of the amalgamating company is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amalgamated company is a new company or the amalgamation proposal provides for a change of the name of the amalgamated company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy of any notice or other documentary evidence that the name has been reserved under section 27(12B) is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a declaration signed by the directors, or proposed directors, of the amalgamated company on the claims of the creditors is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents are filed in the prescribed form with the particulars required in the form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed fee is paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215E(1) the documents filed with the Registrar are those the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the amalgamation proposal that has been approved is filed`
      AND `any solvency statement made under section 215C(2) or 215D(5), as the case may be, is filed`
      AND `any declaration required under section 215C(3) or 215D(6), as the case may be, is filed`
      AND `a declaration signed by the directors of each amalgamating company stating that the amalgamation has been approved in accordance with this Act and the constitution of the amalgamating company is filed`
      AND ((NOT `the amalgamated company is a new company or the amalgamation proposal provides for a change of the name of the amalgamated company`) OR `a copy of any notice or other documentary evidence that the name has been reserved under section 27(12B) is filed`)
      AND `a declaration signed by the directors, or proposed directors, of the amalgamated company on the claims of the creditors is filed`
      AND `the documents are filed in the prescribed form with the particulars required in the form`
      AND `the prescribed fee is paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the following documents must be filed with the Registrar, in the prescribed form with such particulars as may be required in the form, together with payment of the prescribed fee" (a duty not met; the provision's own question; the form and the fee are prescribed outside the sources)

-- (2): "Where the amalgamated company is a new company — (a) section 19(1)(a) and (c) is deemed to have been complied with if, and only if, subsection (1) has been complied with; and (b) the reference to a person named in the constitution as a director or the
-- secretary of the proposed company in section 19(2)(b) includes a reference to a proposed director of the amalgamated company."
-- src:21406 | (2) Where the amalgamated company is a new company —
-- src:21408 | (a) section 19(1)(a) and (c) is deemed to have been complied
-- src:21409 | with if, and only if, subsection (1) has been complied with;
-- src:21410 | and
-- src:21412 | (b) the reference to a person named in the constitution as a
-- src:21413 | director or the secretary of the proposed company in
-- src:21414 | section 19(2)(b) includes a reference to a proposed director
-- src:21415 | of the amalgamated company.
@ref s 215E(2) (src:21406-21415)
GIVEN `the amalgamated company is a new company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (1) has been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215E(2)(a) section 19(1)(a) and (c) is deemed to have been complied with` MEANS
    IF NOT `the amalgamated company is a new company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the amalgamated company is a new company — (a) section 19(1)(a) and (c) is deemed to have been complied with" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b))
    ELSE IF `subsection (1) has been complied with`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is deemed to have been complied with if, and only if, subsection (1) has been complied with" (a gate closed with "only if")

-- src:21406 | (2) Where the amalgamated company is a new company —
-- src:21408 | (a) section 19(1)(a) and (c) is deemed to have been complied
-- src:21409 | with if, and only if, subsection (1) has been complied with;
-- src:21410 | and
-- src:21412 | (b) the reference to a person named in the constitution as a
-- src:21413 | director or the secretary of the proposed company in
-- src:21414 | section 19(2)(b) includes a reference to a proposed director
-- src:21415 | of the amalgamated company.
@ref s 215E(2)(b) (src:21406-21415)
GIVEN `the amalgamated company is a new company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a proposed director of the amalgamated company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215E(2)(b) the person is within the reference in section 19(2)(b) to a person named in the constitution as a director or the secretary` MEANS
    IF NOT `the amalgamated company is a new company`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the amalgamated company is a new company — ... (b) the reference to a person named in the constitution as a director or the secretary of the proposed company in section 19(2)(b) includes" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b))
    ELSE IF `the person is a proposed director of the amalgamated company`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the reference ... in section 19(2)(b) includes a reference to a proposed director of the amalgamated company" leaves the reference open

§ `Section 215F: notice of amalgamation`

-- Heading (line 21419): "Notice of amalgamation, etc.": not operative.

DECLARE `s 215F(1) what the Registrar must issue` IS ONE OF
    `s 215F(1)(a) a notice of amalgamation`
    `s 215F(1)(b) a notice of amalgamation together with the notice of incorporation under section 19(4)`

DECLARE `s 215F(1) the amalgamated company` IS ONE OF
    `s 215F(1)(a) the amalgamated company is the same as one of the amalgamating companies`
    `s 215F(1)(b) the amalgamated company is a new company`
    `s 215F(1) the amalgamated company is some other company`

-- (1): "Upon the receipt of the relevant documents and fees, the Registrar must — (a) if the amalgamated company is the same as one of the amalgamating companies — issue a notice of amalgamation in such form as the Registrar may determine; or
-- (b) if the amalgamated company is a new company — issue a notice of amalgamation in such form as the Registrar may determine together with the notice of incorporation under section 19(4)."
-- src:21421 | 215F.—(1) Upon the receipt of the relevant documents and fees,
-- src:21422 | the Registrar must —
-- src:21424 | (a) if the amalgamated company is the same as one of the
-- src:21425 | amalgamating companies — issue a notice of
-- src:21426 | amalgamation in such form as the Registrar may
-- src:21427 | determine; or
-- src:21432 | (b) if the amalgamated company is a new company — issue a
-- src:21433 | notice of amalgamation in such form as the Registrar may
-- src:21434 | determine together with the notice of incorporation under
-- src:21435 | section 19(4).
@ref s 215F(1) (src:21421-21435)
GIVEN `the Registrar has received the relevant documents and fees` IS A BOOLEAN
      company IS A `s 215F(1) the amalgamated company`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 215F(1) what the Registrar must issue`
`s 215F(1) what the Registrar must issue on receiving the documents and fees` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Registrar has received the relevant documents and fees`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "Upon the receipt of the relevant documents and fees, the Registrar must" (the duty arises on receipt; the subsection says nothing of the Registrar before it)
    ELSE CONSIDER company
         WHEN `s 215F(1)(a) the amalgamated company is the same as one of the amalgamating companies` THEN JUST `s 215F(1)(a) a notice of amalgamation`
         WHEN `s 215F(1)(b) the amalgamated company is a new company` THEN JUST `s 215F(1)(b) a notice of amalgamation together with the notice of incorporation under section 19(4)`
         OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) if the amalgamated company is the same as one of the amalgamating companies ...; or (b) if the amalgamated company is a new company" (the subsection names two cases and says nothing of any other)

-- (2): "Where an amalgamation proposal specifies a date on which the amalgamation is intended to become effective, and that date is the same as or later than the date on which the Registrar receives the relevant documents and fees mentioned in subsection (1),
-- the notice of amalgamation and any notice of incorporation issued by the Registrar must be expressed to have effect on the date specified in the amalgamation proposal."
-- src:21437 | (2) Where an amalgamation proposal specifies a date on which the
-- src:21438 | amalgamation is intended to become effective, and that date is the
-- src:21439 | same as or later than the date on which the Registrar receives the
-- src:21440 | relevant documents and fees mentioned in subsection (1), the notice
-- src:21441 | of amalgamation and any notice of incorporation issued by the
-- src:21442 | Registrar must be expressed to have effect on the date specified in the
-- src:21443 | amalgamation proposal.
@ref s 215F(2) (src:21437-21443)
GIVEN `the amalgamation proposal specifies a date on which the amalgamation is intended to become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date specified` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the Registrar receives the relevant documents and fees` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215F(2) the notice must be expressed to have effect on the date specified in the amalgamation proposal` MEANS
    IF `the amalgamation proposal specifies a date on which the amalgamation is intended to become effective` AND (`the date specified` AT LEAST `the date on which the Registrar receives the relevant documents and fees`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an amalgamation proposal specifies a date on which the amalgamation is intended to become effective, and that date is the same as or later than the date on which the Registrar receives the relevant documents and fees" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b))

-- (3): "The Registrar must, as soon as practicable after the effective date of an amalgamation, remove the amalgamating companies, other than the amalgamated company, from the register." "As soon as practicable" is not a number of days: the regulative rule of 215F(3) takes the section's own standard of time as an input (notes/lest-without-deadline.md).
-- src:21445 | (3) The Registrar must, as soon as practicable after the effective
-- src:21446 | date of an amalgamation, remove the amalgamating companies, other
-- src:21447 | than the amalgamated company, from the register.
@ref s 215F(3) (src:21445-21447)
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the effective date of the amalgamation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215F(3) the Registrar must remove the amalgamating companies, other than the amalgamated company, from the register` MEANS
    IF `the day asked about` GREATER THAN `the effective date of the amalgamation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "as soon as practicable after the effective date of an amalgamation" (the duty runs from after the effective date; the subsection says nothing of a day on or before it)

-- (4): "Upon the application of the amalgamated company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the amalgamated company a certificate of confirmation of amalgamation."
-- src:21449 | (4) Upon the application of the amalgamated company and
-- src:21450 | payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the
-- src:21451 | amalgamated company a certificate of confirmation of
-- src:21452 | amalgamation.
@ref s 215F(4) (src:21449-21452)
GIVEN `the amalgamated company has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prescribed fee has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215F(4) the Registrar must issue a certificate of confirmation of amalgamation to the amalgamated company` MEANS
    IF `the amalgamated company has applied` AND `the prescribed fee has been paid`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the application of the amalgamated company and payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue" ("upon" counts as "where": ruling (c) of 2026-11-05; periods ruling (b); marginal reading (a))

§ `Section 215G: effect of amalgamations`

-- Heading (line 21456): "Effect of amalgamations": not operative.

-- The effects the section lists, and any other.
DECLARE `s 215G effect` IS ONE OF
    `s 215G(a) the amalgamation is effective`
    `s 215G(b) the amalgamated company has the name specified in the amalgamation proposal`
    `s 215G(c) all the property, rights and privileges of each of the amalgamating companies are transferred to and vest in the amalgamated company`
    `s 215G(d) all the liabilities and obligations of each of the amalgamating companies are transferred to and become the liabilities and obligations of the amalgamated company`
    `s 215G(e) all proceedings pending by or against any amalgamating company may be continued by or against the amalgamated company`
    `s 215G(f) any conviction, ruling, order or judgment in favour of or against an amalgamating company may be enforced by or against the amalgamated company`
    `s 215G(g) the shares and rights of the members in the amalgamating companies are converted into the shares and rights provided for in the amalgamation proposal`
    `s 215G some other effect`

GIVEN effect IS A `s 215G effect`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 215G the effect is one the section lists` MEANS
    CONSIDER effect
    WHEN `s 215G some other effect` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- 215G: "On the date shown in a notice of amalgamation — (a) the amalgamation is effective; ...; (g) the shares and rights of the members in the amalgamating companies are converted". On and after the date the effect holds;
-- before it the section says nothing, and an effect it does not list is not addressed.
-- src:21458 | 215G. On the date shown in a notice of amalgamation —
-- src:21460 | (a) the amalgamation is effective;
-- src:21462 | (b) the amalgamated company has the name specified in the
-- src:21463 | amalgamation proposal;
-- src:21465 | (c) all the property, rights and privileges of each of the
-- src:21466 | amalgamating companies are transferred to and vest in the
-- src:21467 | amalgamated company;
-- src:21469 | (d) all the liabilities and obligations of each of the
-- src:21470 | amalgamating companies are transferred to and become
-- src:21471 | the liabilities and obligations of the amalgamated
-- src:21472 | company;
-- src:21474 | (e) all proceedings pending by or against any amalgamating
-- src:21475 | company may be continued by or against the amalgamated
-- src:21476 | company;
-- src:21481 | (f) any conviction, ruling, order or judgment in favour of or
-- src:21482 | against an amalgamating company may be enforced by or
-- src:21483 | against the amalgamated company; and
-- src:21485 | (g) the shares and rights of the members in the amalgamating
-- src:21486 | companies are converted into the shares and rights
-- src:21487 | provided for in the amalgamation proposal.
@ref s 215G (src:21458-21487)
GIVEN effect IS A `s 215G effect`
      `the date shown in the notice of amalgamation` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215G on the date shown in the notice of amalgamation the effect has taken place` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 215G the effect is one the section lists` effect)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the date shown in a notice of amalgamation — (a) ...; (g) ..." (the section lists seven effects and says nothing of any other)
    ELSE IF `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the date shown in the notice of amalgamation`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the date shown in a notice of amalgamation" (the section says what holds on that date and says nothing of an earlier day)

§ `Section 215H: power of the Court`

-- Heading (line 21489): "Power of Court in certain cases": not operative.

DECLARE `s 215H(1) the person` IS ONE OF
    `s 215H(1) a member of an amalgamating company`
    `s 215H(1) a creditor of an amalgamating company`
    `s 215H(1) a person to whom an amalgamating company is under an obligation`
    `s 215H(1) some other person`

GIVEN person IS A `s 215H(1) the person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 215H(1) the person is one the subsection names` MEANS
    CONSIDER person
    WHEN `s 215H(1) some other person` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- (1): "If the Court is satisfied that giving effect to an amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice a member or creditor of an amalgamating company or a person to whom an amalgamating company is under an obligation, it may, on the application of that person
-- made at any time before the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective, make any order it thinks fit in relation to the amalgamation proposal".
-- A grant ("may") with an "if" gate: NOTHING when the Court is not satisfied or the person is not within the three (grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1); JUST FALSE where there is no application or it is out of time ("on the application ... made at any time before":
-- ruling (c) of 2026-11-05 and the periods ruling (a)). Fork F-215H-1.
-- src:21491 | 215H.—(1) If the Court is satisfied that giving effect to an
-- src:21492 | amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice a member or
-- src:21493 | creditor of an amalgamating company or a person to whom an
-- src:21494 | amalgamating company is under an obligation, it may, on the
-- src:21495 | application of that person made at any time before the date on which
-- src:21496 | the amalgamation becomes effective, make any order it thinks fit in
-- src:21497 | relation to the amalgamation proposal, and may, without limiting the
-- src:21498 | generality of this subsection, make an order —
-- src:21500 | (a) directing that effect must not be given to the amalgamation
-- src:21501 | proposal;
-- src:21503 | (b) modifying the amalgamation proposal in such manner as
-- src:21504 | may be specified in the order; or
-- src:21506 | (c) directing the amalgamating company or its board of
-- src:21507 | directors to reconsider the amalgamation proposal or any
-- src:21508 | part thereof.
@ref s 215H(1) (src:21491-21508)
GIVEN `the Court is satisfied that giving effect to the amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 215H(1) the person`
      `that person has applied to the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the application` IS A DATE
      `the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215H(1) the Court may make an order in relation to the amalgamation proposal` MEANS
    IF NOT `that person has applied to the Court`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it may, on the application of that person made at any time before the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective" (split site (ii): "on the application" is read as "upon", which counts as "where": ruling (c) of 2026-11-05; fork F-215H-1)
    ELSE IF `the day of the application` AT LEAST `the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "made at any time before the date on which the amalgamation becomes effective" (a period the text fixes in its own words; periods ruling (a); fork F-215H-1)
         ELSE IF NOT (`s 215H(1) the person is one the subsection names` person)
              THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a member or creditor of an amalgamating company or a person to whom an amalgamating company is under an obligation" (a grant naming three kinds of person and no other)
              ELSE IF `the Court is satisfied that giving effect to the amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice the person`
                   THEN JUST TRUE
                   ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the Court is satisfied that giving effect to an amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice a member or creditor" (a grant with an "if" gate; grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-215H-1)

-- (1)(a) to (c): the orders the section names, "without limiting the generality" of the power: any order the Court thinks fit in relation to the proposal.
DECLARE `s 215H(1) the order` IS ONE OF
    `s 215H(1)(a) an order directing that effect must not be given to the amalgamation proposal`
    `s 215H(1)(b) an order modifying the amalgamation proposal in such manner as may be specified in the order`
    `s 215H(1)(c) an order directing the amalgamating company or its board of directors to reconsider the amalgamation proposal or any part thereof`
    `s 215H(1) any other order in relation to the amalgamation proposal`
    `s 215H(1) an order not in relation to the amalgamation proposal`

-- src:21491 | 215H.—(1) If the Court is satisfied that giving effect to an
-- src:21492 | amalgamation proposal would unfairly prejudice a member or
-- src:21493 | creditor of an amalgamating company or a person to whom an
-- src:21494 | amalgamating company is under an obligation, it may, on the
-- src:21495 | application of that person made at any time before the date on which
-- src:21496 | the amalgamation becomes effective, make any order it thinks fit in
-- src:21497 | relation to the amalgamation proposal, and may, without limiting the
-- src:21498 | generality of this subsection, make an order —
-- src:21500 | (a) directing that effect must not be given to the amalgamation
-- src:21501 | proposal;
-- src:21503 | (b) modifying the amalgamation proposal in such manner as
-- src:21504 | may be specified in the order; or
-- src:21506 | (c) directing the amalgamating company or its board of
-- src:21507 | directors to reconsider the amalgamation proposal or any
-- src:21508 | part thereof.
@ref s 215H(1) orders (src:21491-21508)
GIVEN order IS A `s 215H(1) the order`
      `the Court thinks fit to make the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215H(1) the order is within the Court's power` MEANS
    IF NOT `the Court thinks fit to make the order`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "make any order it thinks fit" (a grant limited by the Court's own judgment; grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-215H-2)
    ELSE CONSIDER order
         WHEN `s 215H(1) an order not in relation to the amalgamation proposal` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "make any order it thinks fit in relation to the amalgamation proposal" (a grant limited to orders in relation to the proposal)
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2): "An order may be made under subsection (1) on such terms or conditions as the Court thinks fit."
-- src:21510 | (2) An order may be made under subsection (1) on such terms or
-- src:21511 | conditions as the Court thinks fit.
@ref s 215H(2) (src:21510-21511)
GIVEN `the Court thinks fit to impose the terms or conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215H(2) the order may be made on the terms or conditions` MEANS
    IF `the Court thinks fit to impose the terms or conditions`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on such terms or conditions as the Court thinks fit" (a grant limited by the Court's own judgment; grant ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1; fork F-215H-2)

§ `Section 215K: money or other consideration held in trust under the terms of the amalgamation`

-- (1): "Where the terms of any amalgamation proposal that is approved under section 215C, or is deemed to be approved under section 215D, provide for any money or other consideration to be held by or on behalf of any party to the amalgamation in trust for any person,
-- the person holding the money or other consideration may, after the expiration of 2 years and must before the expiration of 10 years from the date on which, the money or other consideration was received by the person, transfer the money or other consideration to the Official Receiver."
-- As in section 210(10A): after the 2 years, up to and including the last day of the 10 years. Here "the person" is the person holding it (contrast section 215(6): finding 3 in NOTES.md).
-- src:21666 | 215K.—(1) Where the terms of any amalgamation proposal that is
-- src:21667 | approved under section 215C, or is deemed to be approved under
-- src:21668 | section 215D, provide for any money or other consideration to be
-- src:21669 | held by or on behalf of any party to the amalgamation in trust for any
-- src:21674 | person, the person holding the money or other consideration may,
-- src:21675 | after the expiration of 2 years and must before the expiration of
-- src:21676 | 10 years from the date on which, the money or other consideration
-- src:21677 | was received by the person, transfer the money or other consideration
-- src:21678 | to the Official Receiver.
@ref s 215K(1) (src:21666-21678)
GIVEN `the terms of an amalgamation proposal approved under section 215C or deemed approved under section 215D provide for money or other consideration to be held in trust for a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` IS A DATE
      `the day of the transfer to the Official Receiver` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215K(1) the transfer to the Official Receiver is within the time the subsection allows` MEANS
    IF NOT `the terms of an amalgamation proposal approved under section 215C or deemed approved under section 215D provide for money or other consideration to be held in trust for a person`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the terms of any amalgamation proposal that is approved under section 215C, or is deemed to be approved under section 215D, provide for any money or other consideration to be held" (a "where" condition; periods ruling (b))
    ELSE IF `the day of the transfer to the Official Receiver` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` 2 Years)
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may, after the expiration of 2 years" (a period the text fixes in its own words; a transfer on or before the last day of the 2 years is too early; periods ruling (a))
         ELSE IF `the day of the transfer to the Official Receiver` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` 10 Years)
              THEN JUST TRUE
              ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must before the expiration of 10 years from the date on which, the money or other consideration was received" (a period the text fixes in its own words; a transfer after the last day of the 10 years is late; periods ruling (a))

GIVEN `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` IS A DATE
      `the start day of the trace` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 215K(1) the number of days from the start day to the last day before the 10 years expire` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the money or other consideration was received by the person holding it` 10 Years) MINUS `the start day of the trace`

-- (2): "The Official Receiver must (a) deal with any moneys received under subsection (1) as if the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018; and
-- (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under subsection (1) in such manner as the Official Receiver thinks fit and must deal with the proceeds ... as if it were moneys paid ... under section 197".
DECLARE `s 215K(2) treatment` IS ONE OF
    `s 215K(2)(a) dealt with as if the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 215K(2)(b) sold or disposed of in the manner the Official Receiver thinks fit, the proceeds dealt with as if moneys paid under section 197 of that Act`

-- src:21682 | (2) The Official Receiver must —
-- src:21684 | (a) deal with any moneys received under subsection (1) as if
-- src:21685 | the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under
-- src:21686 | section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:21687 | Dissolution Act 2018; and
-- src:21689 | (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under
-- src:21690 | subsection (1) in such manner as the Official Receiver
-- src:21691 | thinks fit and must deal with the proceeds of such sale or
-- src:21692 | disposal as if it were moneys paid to the Official Receiver
-- src:21693 | under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:21694 | Dissolution Act 2018.
@ref s 215K(2) (src:21682-21694)
GIVEN `the thing received under subsection (1) is money` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the thing received under subsection (1) is other consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 215K(2) treatment`
`s 215K(2) how the Official Receiver must deal with what is received under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the thing received under subsection (1) is money`
    THEN JUST `s 215K(2)(a) dealt with as if the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    ELSE IF `the thing received under subsection (1) is other consideration`
         THEN JUST `s 215K(2)(b) sold or disposed of in the manner the Official Receiver thinks fit, the proceeds dealt with as if moneys paid under section 197 of that Act`
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) deal with any moneys received under subsection (1) ...; and (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under subsection (1)" (the subsection says what the Official Receiver does with money and with other consideration received under (1), and nothing of anything else)

§ `Regulative rules: the duties of ss 215A to 215K that name a party and an act`

-- The board of directors of an amalgamating company: not a constructor of the core's `Party` (NEEDS-CORE.md), so a party of this module's own.
DECLARE `s 215C party` IS ONE OF
    `s 215C the board of directors of an amalgamating company` HAS `s 215C the name of the amalgamating company` IS A STRING

DECLARE `s 215C act` IS ONE OF
    `s 215C(2)(a) resolve that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the amalgamating company`
    `s 215C(2)(b) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating company in accordance with section 215I`
    `s 215C(2)(c) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company in accordance with section 215J`
    `s 215C(3) sign a declaration stating that, in the director's opinion, the conditions are satisfied, and the grounds for that opinion`
    `s 215C(4) send to every member a copy of the amalgamation proposal, a copy of the declarations, a statement of material interests and such further information as is necessary`
    `s 215C(5)(a) send a copy of the amalgamation proposal to every secured creditor of the amalgamating company`
    `s 215C(5)(b) cause to be published in at least one daily English newspaper circulating generally in Singapore a notice of the proposed amalgamation`
    `s 215D(3) give written notice of the proposed amalgamation to every secured creditor of the amalgamating company`
    `s 215D(5) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated company in accordance with section 215J`
    `s 215D(6) sign a declaration stating that, in the director's opinion, the conditions specified in section 215J(1)(a) and (b) are satisfied, and the grounds for that opinion`
    `s 215F(1)(a) issue a notice of amalgamation`
    `s 215F(1)(b) issue a notice of amalgamation together with the notice of incorporation under section 19(4)`
    `s 215F(3) remove the amalgamating companies, other than the amalgamated company, from the register`
    `s 215F(4) issue to the amalgamated company a certificate of confirmation of amalgamation`
    `s 215K(1) transfer the money or other consideration to the Official Receiver`

DECLARE `s 215K(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 215K(2)(a) deal with the moneys received under subsection (1) as if they were paid under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    `s 215K(2)(b) sell or dispose of the other consideration and deal with the proceeds as if they were moneys paid under section 197 of that Act`

-- 215C(2): the board's three duties before the general meeting. The deadline is the day before the meeting (see the layer-1 function: the day of the meeting itself cannot be placed from a date).
-- src:21175 | (2) The board of directors of each amalgamating company must,
-- src:21176 | before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) —
-- src:21178 | (a) resolve that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the
-- src:21179 | amalgamating company;
-- src:21181 | (b) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamating
-- src:21182 | company in accordance with section 215I; and
-- src:21184 | (c) make a solvency statement in relation to the amalgamated
-- src:21185 | company in accordance with section 215J.
@ref s 215C(2) rule (a) (src:21175-21185)
GIVEN `the name of the amalgamating company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from the start of the trace to the day before the general meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 215C party` `s 215C act`
`s 215C(2)(a) the board must resolve before the general meeting that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the amalgamating company` MEANS
    PARTY `s 215C the board of directors of an amalgamating company` `the name of the amalgamating company`
    MUST `s 215C(2)(a) resolve that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the amalgamating company`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the start of the trace to the day before the general meeting`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 215C the board of directors of an amalgamating company` `the name of the amalgamating company` BECAUSE "the board did not resolve before the general meeting that the amalgamation is in the best interest of the amalgamating company"

-- src:21175 | (2) The board of directors of each amalgamating company must,
