-- 215C(3): the director signs the declaration. No time stated: the time allowed is the s 52 input `the period of all convenient speed, as found` (notes/lest-without-deadline.md), so a late act reaches BREACH.
-- src:21190 | (3) Every director who votes in favour of the resolution and the
-- src:21191 | making of the statements mentioned in subsection (2) must sign a
-- src:21192 | declaration stating —
-- src:21194 | (a) that, in his or her opinion, the conditions specified in
-- src:21195 | subsection (2)(a), section 215I(1)(a) and (b) (in relation to
-- src:21196 | the amalgamating company) and section 215J(1)(a) and (b)
-- src:21197 | (in relation to the amalgamated company) are satisfied; and
-- src:21199 | (b) the grounds for that opinion.
@ref s 215C(3) rule (src:21190-21199)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215C act`
`s 215C(3) a director who votes in favour must sign the declaration` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 215C(3) sign a declaration stating that, in the director's opinion, the conditions are satisfied, and the grounds for that opinion`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not sign a declaration stating that, in the director's opinion, the conditions are satisfied, and the grounds for that opinion"

-- 215C(4): the board must send to every member not less than 21 days before the meeting: a deadline.
-- src:21201 | (4) The board of directors of each amalgamating company must
-- src:21202 | send to every member of the amalgamating company, not less than
-- src:21203 | 21 days before the general meeting mentioned in subsection (1)(a) —
-- src:21205 | (a) a copy of the amalgamation proposal;
-- src:21207 | (b) a copy of the declarations given by the directors under
-- src:21208 | subsection (3);
-- src:21210 | (c) a statement of any material interests of the directors,
-- src:21211 | whether in that capacity or otherwise; and
-- src:21213 | (d) such further information and explanation as may be
-- src:21214 | necessary to enable a reasonable member of the
-- src:21215 | amalgamating company to understand the nature and
-- src:21216 | implications, for the amalgamating company and its
-- src:21217 | members, of the proposed amalgamation.
@ref s 215C(4) rule (src:21201-21217)
GIVEN `the name of the amalgamating company` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day for the sending` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 215C party` `s 215C act`
`s 215C(4) the board must send what the subsection requires to every member at least 21 days before the general meeting` MEANS
    PARTY `s 215C the board of directors of an amalgamating company` `the name of the amalgamating company`
    MUST `s 215C(4) send to every member a copy of the amalgamation proposal, a copy of the declarations, a statement of material interests and such further information as is necessary`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day for the sending`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 215C the board of directors of an amalgamating company` `the name of the amalgamating company` BECAUSE "the board did not send what the subsection requires to every member not less than 21 days before the general meeting"

