-- 215F(1): the Registrar must issue a notice: (a) if the amalgamated company is one of the amalgamating companies; (b) if it is a new company. "Upon the receipt" is a trigger, not a number: (a) takes the s 52 input `the period of all convenient speed, as found`, so a late notice reaches BREACH; (b) is issued together with the s 19(4) notice, whose time it follows, and has none of its own (OTHER; notes/lest-without-deadline.md).
-- src:21421 | 215F.—(1) Upon the receipt of the relevant documents and fees,
-- src:21422 | the Registrar must —
-- src:21424 | (a) if the amalgamated company is the same as one of the
-- src:21425 | amalgamating companies — issue a notice of
-- src:21426 | amalgamation in such form as the Registrar may
-- src:21427 | determine; or
-- src:21432 | (b) if the amalgamated company is a new company — issue a
-- src:21433 | notice of amalgamation in such form as the Registrar may
-- src:21434 | determine together with the notice of incorporation under
-- src:21435 | section 19(4).
@ref s 215F(1) rule (src:21421-21435)
GIVEN `the amalgamated company is a new company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215C act`
`s 215F(1) the Registrar must issue the notice of amalgamation on receiving the documents and fees` MEANS
    IF `the amalgamated company is a new company`
    THEN PARTY Registrar
         MUST `s 215F(1)(b) issue a notice of amalgamation together with the notice of incorporation under section 19(4)`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         -- no LEST: no deadline is modelled for this duty; dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not issue a notice of amalgamation together with the notice of incorporation under section 19(4)" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]
    ELSE PARTY Registrar
         MUST `s 215F(1)(a) issue a notice of amalgamation`
         WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not issue a notice of amalgamation"

-- 215F(3): "as soon as practicable" is not a number of days: the section's own standard of time is the input `the period the standard of time allows, as found`, so a late act reaches BREACH (notes/lest-without-deadline.md).
-- src:21445 | (3) The Registrar must, as soon as practicable after the effective
-- src:21446 | date of an amalgamation, remove the amalgamating companies, other
-- src:21447 | than the amalgamated company, from the register.
@ref s 215F(3) rule (src:21445-21447)
GIVEN `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("as soon as practicable") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215C act`
`s 215F(3) the Registrar must remove the amalgamating companies from the register` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 215F(3) remove the amalgamating companies, other than the amalgamated company, from the register`
    WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section's own standard: "as soon as practicable" (s 215F(3)); the period is an input, as found (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not remove the amalgamating companies, other than the amalgamated company, from the register"

-- src:21449 | (4) Upon the application of the amalgamated company and
-- src:21450 | payment of the prescribed fee, the Registrar must issue to the
-- src:21451 | amalgamated company a certificate of confirmation of
-- src:21452 | amalgamation.
@ref s 215F(4) rule (src:21449-21452)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215C act`
`s 215F(4) the Registrar must issue the certificate of confirmation of amalgamation` MEANS
    PARTY Registrar
    MUST `s 215F(4) issue to the amalgamated company a certificate of confirmation of amalgamation`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Registrar BECAUSE "the Registrar did not issue to the amalgamated company a certificate of confirmation of amalgamation"

-- 215K(1): the person holding the money must transfer before the expiration of 10 years: a deadline.
-- src:21666 | 215K.—(1) Where the terms of any amalgamation proposal that is
-- src:21667 | approved under section 215C, or is deemed to be approved under
-- src:21668 | section 215D, provide for any money or other consideration to be
-- src:21669 | held by or on behalf of any party to the amalgamation in trust for any
-- src:21674 | person, the person holding the money or other consideration may,
-- src:21675 | after the expiration of 2 years and must before the expiration of
-- src:21676 | 10 years from the date on which, the money or other consideration
-- src:21677 | was received by the person, transfer the money or other consideration
-- src:21678 | to the Official Receiver.
@ref s 215K(1) rule (src:21666-21678)
GIVEN who IS A Party
      `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day before the 10 years expire` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 215C act`
`s 215K(1) the person holding the money or other consideration must transfer it to the Official Receiver before the 10 years expire` MEANS
    PARTY who
    MUST `s 215K(1) transfer the money or other consideration to the Official Receiver`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the start of the trace to the last day before the 10 years expire`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY who BECAUSE "the money or other consideration was not transferred to the Official Receiver before the expiration of 10 years from the date it was received"

-- 215K(2): the Official Receiver's duties. No time stated: the time allowed is the s 52 input `the period of all convenient speed, as found` (notes/lest-without-deadline.md), so a late act reaches BREACH.
-- src:21682 | (2) The Official Receiver must —
-- src:21684 | (a) deal with any moneys received under subsection (1) as if
-- src:21685 | the moneys were paid to the Official Receiver under
-- src:21686 | section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:21687 | Dissolution Act 2018; and
-- src:21689 | (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under
-- src:21690 | subsection (1) in such manner as the Official Receiver
-- src:21691 | thinks fit and must deal with the proceeds of such sale or
-- src:21692 | disposal as if it were moneys paid to the Official Receiver
-- src:21693 | under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:21694 | Dissolution Act 2018.
@ref s 215K(2) rule (src:21682-21694)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 210(10B) party` `s 215K(2) act`
`s 215K(2)(a) the Official Receiver must deal with the moneys as if they were paid under section 197` MEANS
    PARTY `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver`
    MUST `s 215K(2)(a) deal with the moneys received under subsection (1) as if they were paid under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and Dissolution Act 2018`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver` BECAUSE "the moneys received under subsection (1) were not dealt with as if paid under section 197"

-- src:21689 | (b) sell or dispose of any other consideration received under
-- src:21690 | subsection (1) in such manner as the Official Receiver
-- src:21691 | thinks fit and must deal with the proceeds of such sale or
-- src:21692 | disposal as if it were moneys paid to the Official Receiver
-- src:21693 | under section 197 of the Insolvency, Restructuring and
-- src:21694 | Dissolution Act 2018.
@ref s 215K(2)(b) rule (src:21689-21694)
GIVEN `the period of all convenient speed, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that make up all convenient speed for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 210(10B) party` `s 215K(2) act`
`s 215K(2)(b) the Official Receiver must sell or dispose of the other consideration` MEANS
    PARTY `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver`
    MUST `s 215K(2)(b) sell or dispose of the other consideration and deal with the proceeds as if they were moneys paid under section 197 of that Act`
    WITHIN `the period of all convenient speed, as found`   -- Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed", found as an input (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 210(10B) the Official Receiver` BECAUSE "the other consideration received under subsection (1) was not sold or disposed of, or its proceeds were not dealt with as moneys paid under section 197"
